(7742363, 1276929, 83313, '<td valign="top">A very unique interpretation of the topic, with hair used as a descriptor rather than literally. Borderline shoehorn, but I''ve done my fair share of those myself. Extra pointage for outside the box thinking. <br/> <br/>One minor criticism is that this seems a bit flat. Just not a lot of what I think of as "pop" to the image. Out of curiosity, I did a screen grab and tried a levels adjust on it. I found that the dynamic range was good, stretching all the way from dark to light, but no tones were significantly higher than anything else, which I think is accounting for that appearance.</td>', 'A very unique interpretation of the topic, with hair used as a descriptor rather than literally. Borderline shoehorn, but I''ve done my fair share of those myself. Extra pointage for outside the box thinking.  One minor criticism is that this seems a bit flat. Just not a lot of what I think of as "pop" to the image. Out of curiosity, I did a screen grab and tried a levels adjust on it. I found that the dynamic range was good, stretching all the way from dark to light, but no tones were significantly higher than anything else, which I think is accounting for that appearance.', '2023-04-16 12:53:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7742364, 1277171, 83313, '<td valign="top">I guess in an urban environment, magenta WOULD be camouflaged! I''m sure you were referring to the green hair, but my eye landed on the chick on the back.</td>', 'I guess in an urban environment, magenta WOULD be camouflaged! I''m sure you were referring to the green hair, but my eye landed on the chick on the back.', '2023-04-16 12:55:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7742365, 1277246, 83313, '<td valign="top">Cousin It is my favorite!</td>', 'Cousin It is my favorite!', '2023-04-16 12:55:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7742366, 1276975, 83313, '<td valign="top">I have a strong suspicion whose entry this is and I know you have requested feedback, so here are a handful of things I noticed:<br/>-The image is pretty flat looking. Not a lot of variations in tonal range. A levels adjustment would take care of a lot of that, giving the image more detail and visual pop.<br/>-What look like creases in the background image are pulling my eye away from the adorable doggo. <br/>-That pink background may have also affected the auto white balance for the main subject, which isn''t terrible, but looks a little off. A fix for that going forward could be to shoot in RAW. It requires more work in post processing, but offers a lot of control over both white balance and to pull in detail from clipped highlights and shadows that would be lost in a JPG.<br/>-The crop is a little tight, especially at the bottom. It leads my eye through the image in an odd way. Perhaps having a bit more room at the bottom under the dog''s chin would help that.<br/> <br/>Sorry to be so harsh, but if this is from whom I think, I know you wanted feedback.</td>', 'I have a strong suspicion whose entry this is and I know you have requested feedback, so here are a handful of things I noticed:-The image is pretty flat looking. Not a lot of variations in tonal range. A levels adjustment would take care of a lot of that, giving the image more detail and visual pop.-What look like creases in the background image are pulling my eye away from the adorable doggo. -That pink background may have also affected the auto white balance for the main subject, which isn''t terrible, but looks a little off. A fix for that going forward could be to shoot in RAW. It requires more work in post processing, but offers a lot of control over both white balance and to pull in detail from clipped highlights and shadows that would be lost in a JPG.-The crop is a little tight, especially at the bottom. It leads my eye through the image in an odd way. Perhaps having a bit more room at the bottom under the dog''s chin would help that. Sorry to be so harsh, but if this is from whom I think, I know you wanted feedback.', '2023-04-16 13:10:27.000000', NULL, 1),
